<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khalifa bin Zayed Al Nahyan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1948–2022</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a> bin Zayed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-nahyan">Al Nahyan</a> was ruler of Abu Dhabi and president of the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a> from November 2004 until his death in May 2022, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zayed-bin-sultan-al-nahyan">Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan</a>. Formerly crown prince and chairman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-dhabi-investment-authority">Abu Dhabi Investment Authority</a>, he presided over rapid growth and backed Dubai financially during its 2009 debt crisis, after which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burj-khalifa">Burj Khalifa</a> was named after him. After a stroke in 2014 his half-brother Mohamed bin Zayed held effective power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khalifa-bin-zayed-al-nahyan.jpg" alt="Khalifa bin Zayed Al Nahyan" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Helene C. Stikkel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khalifa_Bin_Zayed_Al_Nahyan-CROPPED.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
